[
    {
        "content": "<p>I am working on adding support for customizing the WIT package dependency directory path like:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"n\">wit_bindgen</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">generate</span><span class=\"o\">!</span><span class=\"p\">({</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"../wit\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deps</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"s\">\"../wit-deps\"</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">});</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>At the moment the deps directory is hardcoded in <code>wit-parser</code>'s internal <code>Resolve::_push_dir</code> method:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Rust\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"k\">fn</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nf\">_push_dir</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"k\">mut</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kp\">&amp;</span><span class=\"nc\">Path</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">-&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"nb\">Result</span><span class=\"o\">&lt;</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"k\">super</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">PackageId</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PackageSourceMap</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">&gt;</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">{</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">top_pkg</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parse_dir</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">with_context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"fm\">format!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"failed to parse package: {}\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">display</span><span class=\"p\">()))</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deps</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">path</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">join</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"deps\"</span><span class=\"p\">);</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deps</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">parse_deps_dir</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">&amp;</span><span class=\"n\">deps</span><span class=\"p\">)</span>\n<span class=\"w\">        </span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">with_context</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"o\">||</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"fm\">format!</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"s\">\"failed to parse dependency directory: {}\"</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deps</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">display</span><span class=\"p\">()))</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"kd\">let</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">pkg_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">self</span><span class=\"p\">.</span><span class=\"n\">sort_unresolved_packages</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">top_pkg</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">deps</span><span class=\"p\">)</span><span class=\"o\">?</span><span class=\"p\">;</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"nb\">Ok</span><span class=\"p\">((</span><span class=\"n\">pkg_id</span><span class=\"p\">,</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">PackageSourceMap</span><span class=\"p\">::</span><span class=\"n\">from_inner</span><span class=\"p\">(</span><span class=\"n\">inner</span><span class=\"p\">)))</span>\n<span class=\"p\">}</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>I would solve this by adding <code>deps: impl AsRef&lt;Path&gt;</code> as a parameter to the internal <code>_push_dir</code> method.</p>\n<p>My question is if I should update the public <code>push_dir</code> method as well or if I should create a new <code>push_dir_with_deps</code> method instead?</p>\n<hr>\n<p>Another question is then how we actually use this. As wit-bindgen relies on <code>Resolve::push_path</code>.</p>\n<p>I am of the opinion to have wit-bindgen use <code>Resolve::push_dir_with_deps</code> in case a user provided a custom value for <code>deps</code> and <code>path</code> is a directory.</p>\n<p>We could of course update <code>Resolve::push_path</code> as well but that would break a lot of things.</p>\n<p>Let me know what you guys think is the best way forward.</p>\n<p>Related GitHub issue: <a href=\"https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wit-bindgen/issues/1675\">https://github.com/bytecodealliance/wit-bindgen/issues/1675</a></p>",
        "id": 626609106,
        "sender_full_name": "Celarye",
        "timestamp": 1790254280
    },
